{#
    Rows for the gutter grid. Every list on the site that pairs an entry in
    the main column with a short fact in the margin column is built from
    these, so the titles line up down the page and the facts line up beside
    them. The fact comes after the entry in the markup: a screen reader hears
    the title first, as the eye reads it, and the CSS places each in its
    column. (The class keeps the name "gutter" from when the fact sat to the
    left of the entry.)

    `entryRow` is the two-line form: a title with a summary under it, used by
    the working and reading sections. `href` is optional — the work list passes
    none, so a role renders as plain text rather than as a link to nowhere.
    `quietGutter` keeps the gutter's text in the accessibility tree while
    taking it out of the visual column; see the work list for why.

    `postRow` is the one-line form: a linked title and its date. The date is
    month and year only, in the same tracked caps as every other date on the
    site; the full date is kept for the post itself.

    `projectRow` leads with a picture: a crop of the project's cover, or of
    its `thumbnail` when the cover is too dark to read that small, beside the
    title and summary, with the year in the margin where every other list
    keeps its date. The thumbnail's alt is empty because the title beside it
    already names the project. `thumbnailFocus` is an optional
    object-position for the crop (say "50% 15%"), for a picture whose subject
    sits off-centre in the phone strip.
#}
{% macro entryRow(gutter, title, summary = null, href = null, quietGutter = false) %}
<li class="gutter-grid__row">
    <span class="gutter-grid__entry">
        <span class="gutter-grid__title">{% if href %}<a href="{{ href }}">{{ title }}</a>{% else %}{{ title }}{% endif %}</span>
        {%- if summary %}
        <span class="gutter-grid__summary">{{ summary }}</span>
        {%- endif %}
    </span>
    <span class="gutter-grid__gutter gutter-grid__gutter--strong{% if quietGutter %} gutter-grid__gutter--quiet{% endif %}">{{ gutter }}</span>
</li>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro projectRow(item) %}
<li class="gutter-grid__row gutter-grid__row--project">
    <span class="gutter-grid__thumb"{% if item.data.thumbnailFocus %} style="--thumb-focus: {{ item.data.thumbnailFocus }}"{% endif %}><img src="{{ item.data.thumbnail or item.data.cover }}" alt="" eleventy:widths="240,480,800" sizes="(min-width: 720px) 11rem, 100vw"></span>
    <span class="gutter-grid__entry">
        <span class="gutter-grid__title"><a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.data.title }}</a></span>
        <span class="gutter-grid__summary">{{ item.data.description }}</span>
    </span>
    <span class="gutter-grid__gutter gutter-grid__gutter--date">{{ item.data.year | projectDate }}</span>
</li>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro postRow(item) %}
<li class="gutter-grid__row">
    <span class="gutter-grid__title"><a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.data.title }}</a></span>
    <time class="gutter-grid__gutter gutter-grid__gutter--date" datetime="{{ item.date | w3Date }}">{{ item.date | monthYear }}</time>
</li>
{% endmacro %}
